{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the men took hold</b>. Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 19:16) said that \"וַיַּחֲזִיקוּ\" means that he was afraid and had no strength to flee. But the correct interpretation is that it is like \"and Egypt pressed the people hard, to hasten to send them out of the land\" (Exodus 12:33) — so too here, they were pulling them along forcefully to hasten to send them out." "<b>in HaShem's compassion for him</b>. Not by his own merit, but through the compassion of El and His abundant mercy. Or one may say that they seized hold of him to hasten to bring them out while the compassion was still upon him, lest the wrath go forth from before HaShem and increase."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:52.546519503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}